// CotSC Batch 18 - extracted original English dialogue for beregost_citizens.d
// Keep existing @ numbers stable when translating.
@1 = ~I recommend you visit Burning Wizard tavern. They have the best ale in whole Beregost. I assure you, it tastes... different.~
@2 = ~We don't want your kind here. Adventurers! Phi. You meddle with things beyond your comprehension and poison children's mind with dangerous ideas.~
@3 = ~Roads aren't safe anymore. This young boy, Shelligh is playing on me nerves. Constantly walking in and out of nearby forests. He's gon get himself killed, that lad.~
@4 = ~I was suppose to play hide and seek with Shelligh but as usual he is running late. Mom says I am very impatient if I don't get what I want instantly. Do you think so too?~
@5 = ~Plenty of adventurers goes through our town as of late. If you're heading down south to the Nashkel mines be prepared. The roads are treacherous.~
@6 = ~The rumours about war in Amn are really wearing me down. I don't remember last night when I slept for longer than few minutes. I get so worried over this.~
@7 = ~Watch where you going, peasant!~
@8 = ~Don't eavesdrop on us.~
@9 = ~Please, let us talk in peace stranger.~
@10 = ~Please. Leave my room.~
@11 = ~Watch out for old Gurke. He's been a little loony since he lost his cloak to a group of taslois. He's a good lad but... he gets frustrated real quick.~
